From AD&D Monster Manual, Juiblex is one of four demon lords (arguably
the most wimpy of the four; 88 hps from AD&D, not sure about nethack).
He (it?) is know as the "Faceless Lord" because of his amorphous,
slimy, pudding-like appearance (though if I remember, he does have two
eyes from his mug-shot in the AD&D MM).  He is the lord of slimes,
jellies, puddings and those sort of beasties.  In NH, you summon
demons by sacrificing human corpses.  The summoned demons are
peaceful.  Demon lords are untameable, but it may be able to tame
lower demons with scrolls (not sure about this).  Just leave Juiblex
there (and be careful if you are wielding Stormy near him; one wrong
move could mean your death).  The only real benefit of summoning demon
lords is that you don't have to fight them later.

On a somewhat related note, does anyone know if the AD&D demon
lords/arch devils were taken from some mythology?  Obviously,
Baazelbul is close to Baazelbub (sp). But, for example, is there a
Demogorgon-like creature roaming around in books prior to AD&D?
